                            <comment id="16744027" author="agoncharuk" created="Wed, 16 Jan 2019 13:17:44 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=v.pyatkov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;v.pyatkov&quot;&gt;v.pyatkov&lt;/a&gt;, when I run the test, it dumps a lot of warning about a critical thread being blocked, is that something that is supposed to happen? If so, I would like to ignore this critical failure in the test not to dump threads every 5 seconds. Also, 40 seconds for such a test is too long, we need to reduce the test execution time.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16746222" author="v.pyatkov" created="Fri, 18 Jan 2019 12:03:05 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=agoncharuk&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;agoncharuk&quot;&gt;agoncharuk&lt;/a&gt;, thank for the comment.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I have reduced test execution time four times.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;About a lot of warning: Yes, this is supposed behavior, because it the test blocks rebalancing procedure, until &lt;tt&gt;GirdClient&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;has&#160;not connected.&lt;br/&gt;
I modified timeout (&lt;tt&gt;SystemWorkerBlockedTimeout&lt;/tt&gt;) for to hid warnings.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Look at rerun Cache1 suit:&lt;br/&gt;
